---
import DiagramFigure from './DiagramFigure.astro'

// A golden case tests the agent the way a flash card tests a student: one prompt,
// one answer, no memory, no momentum. Real conversations are a tree that branches
// at every reply, and the failures that matter live down a path no author would
// think to write. The left is the unit a person can author and review; the right
// is the space that unit cannot cover.

const levels = [
  ['upgrade?'],
  ['hesitates', 'commits'],
  ['cheaper?', 'cancel?', 'confirm', 'refund?'],
]

const ariaLabel =
  'Two ways to think about a test case. On the left, a flash card: one question, "Is my plan capped?", one gold answer, "No". One prompt, one answer, no memory, no momentum, the unit a subject-matter expert can author and review. On the right, a conversation drawn as a tree that branches at every reply: one opening turn fans into hesitates or commits, and each of those fans again into cheaper, cancel, confirm, refund, and on. The space of conversations is not a list you can author; it is a tree, and the failures that matter live down a path no author would think to write.'
---

<DiagramFigure label="A flash card, and the tree it cannot cover" ariaLabel={ariaLabel} data-ft>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 items-start">
    <div>
      <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted mb-2">The golden case: a flash card</span>
      <div class="ft-card rounded border px-4 py-4">
        <p class="m-0 text-sm text-text-primary"><span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">Q</span> Is my plan capped?</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-sm text-text-primary"><span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">A</span> No.</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-3 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">one prompt, one answer, no memory, no momentum</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted mb-2">A conversation: a branching tree</span>
      <div class="ft-tree space-y-2">
        {
          levels.map((row, i) => (
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2" data-level={i}>
              {row.map((n) => (
                <span class="ft-node font-mono text-mono-xs rounded border px-2 py-1">{n}</span>
              ))}
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <p class="m-0 mt-1 text-center font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">branches at every reply &hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="note">
    A subject-matter expert can review one question and one gold answer and agree it is correct. Nobody
    can author a six-turn conversation with a mind-changer, review it, and be confident it covers the
    right ground. The static set covers the failures you wrote down; conversations supply the rest.
  </Fragment>
</DiagramFigure>

<style is:global>
  [data-ft] .ft-card {
    border-color: var(--color-border-dark);
    background: var(--color-surface-container-low);
  }
  [data-ft] .ft-node {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 5%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
</style>
